meta {
  name: List Unlinked Contacts
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/clients/unlinked?kind=contacts&page=1&pageSize=25
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  kind: contacts
  page: 1
  pageSize: 25
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns a paginated envelope discriminated by kind", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.kind).to.equal("contacts");
    expect(body.items).to.be.an("array");
  });

  test("the envelope is internally consistent", function () {
    // Always runs, whatever the seed holds: a page never exceeds its own size,
    // and `totalPages` is derived from `total`, never reported independently.
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.items.length).to.be.at.most(body.pageSize);
    expect(body.totalPages).to.equal(
      Math.max(1, Math.ceil(body.total / body.pageSize)),
    );
  });

  test("agrees with the count on the chip", function () {
    const counted = bru.getVar("unlinkedContactCount");
    if (counted !== undefined) {
      expect(res.getBody().total).to.equal(counted);
    }
  });

  test("rows carry one email and one phone, never arrays", function () {
    const items = res.getBody().items;
    if (items.length > 0) {
      const row = items[0];
      expect(row).to.have.property("email");
      expect(row).to.have.property("phone");
      expect(row.email).to.not.be.an("array");
      expect(row.phone).to.not.be.an("array");
      // Gone with PAC-91 §5 — membership is a join collection, not a field.
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("householdId");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("isPrimary");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("roleInHousehold");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("isTestRecord");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("agencyId");
    }
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /clients/unlinked?kind=contacts

  People who are **not a current member of any household** (PAC-91 §10).

  - **Module:** `clients`
  - **Permission:** `clients:read`
  - **Data scope:** `own` collapses to **branch**

  ## What "unlinked" means here
  An **anti-join**, not a field test. Since PAC-91 §5 a contact carries no
  household of its own — membership is a row in `householdMembers` — so this is
  the absence of a row with `endedAt: null`. Somebody who *left* every household
  they were in is therefore listed, which is right: the book no longer connects
  them to anything.

  ## Response
  `{ kind, page, pageSize, total, totalPages, items: UnlinkedContactRow[] }`

  A row is `id`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `email`, `phone`, `dateOfBirth`,
  `deceasedAt`, `createdAt`. **One** email and **one** phone — the arrays this
  whole ticket is about are gone (§1). `dateOfBirth` is an ISO instant;
  `deceasedAt` is a calendar `YYYY-MM-DD`, the same split every PAC-91 response
  makes.

  Rows exclude `isTestRecord` contacts.

  ## What the client does with a row
  Nothing, yet — and the row is deliberately **not** a link. There is no contact
  page, and no UI attaches an *existing* contact to a household (the Household
  page's "+ Member" dialog creates a new one). That gap is the finding this list
  surfaces; filling it is a separate ticket.

  ## Errors
  | Status | When |
  |---|---|
  | 400 | `kind` missing or outside the vocabulary, `page`/`pageSize` out of bounds |
  | 401 | Missing/expired bearer token |
  | 403 | `clients` disabled, or the caller lacks `clients:read` |
}
